WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.467
-Thank you for being here, bud.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.534
We've done bits before, but it's
the first time on the couch,

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:06.267
so I'm happy that
you're here talking to me.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:07.534
Thank you very much.
-Oh, about time.

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:09.901
I've been waiting.
-Oh, yeah, please.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.434
Let's talk about been waiting,

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.734
because you re-signed
with the Yankees.

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:14.834
It was a big --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:18.567
Yes. Thank you again.
We're so happy.

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:20.434
A nine-year contract.
-Yep.

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:21.868
-Nine-year contract.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:25.234
Talk to me about
the free-agency decision.

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:27.801
What goes -- Was there ever
a time in your head you go,

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:30.834
"Well, maybe I might not be
back in New York"?

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.400
-Wow.
-I know.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.567
I'm asking the hard-hitting
questions right off the bat.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.167
-No. It was a fun process.

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:38.234
You know, every athlete wants to
get to that position where

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.734
they can kind of choose,
you know, where --

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:42.100
you know, where
they get to play, you know?

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.767
And -- You know, it just so
happened I got drafted by

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.367
the best team,
you know, on the planet,

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.200
so it kind of --
It made the --

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:52.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:53.567
It --

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.133
-But there had to have been
other things,

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:57.534
because you just kept crushing
and crushing and crushing,

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.067
and then, all of a sudden,
everyone was like, "Hey, Aaron.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:00.434
Remember me?"

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.300
Like, "We'd like to
talk to you."

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.767
-Yeah, you know,
I met a lot of great teams,

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:05.801
a lot of great people
along the way,

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:07.567
but, you know,
after every meeting, you know,

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.801
I'd sit down with my wife,

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.634
and we kind of look at each
other and be like,

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:11.801
"We're Yankees."

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:13.334
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
That's good. Yeah.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:16.901
You are. I'm so happy.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:19.467
-There was one teammate
in particular

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:20.934
that helped you
with your decision.

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:22.801
Is that Rizzo?

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:24.167
-Yeah, it was Anthony Rizzo.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:26.767
He played a big part, big part.
He was a free agent, too.

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:29.367
He opted out, but he got
his contract out of the way

00:01:29.367 --> 00:01:32.434
and he said, "Now we got to
get you locked in," so...

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:33.567
-Really?

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:35.234
-He was calling me every day.

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:37.133
He was sending me
texts every day.

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:38.200
-Every day?
-Yeah.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.167
It was -- He was working hard.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.934
-He really did
a good job working --

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:45.334
But then I think that sealed
the deal is your --

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:48.300
Not only are you guys friends,
but your dogs are friends.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.868
-Yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:52.968
-It always comes down
to your pet, right?

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:54.934
-Yeah, he went for the --
He went for my heart.

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:56.200
So he went for --

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.100
You know, my little Penny
and his dog, Kevin,

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.467
are the best of friends.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:01.601
-They're the best of friends.

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:02.667
Penny and --
-Got a picture. There we go.

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:03.701
-Here's a picture. Yeah.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:04.868
-This is what
I had to deal with.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.934
Every day,
I was getting photos like this.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.667
-Now, who is who?

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.200
-I got Penny right here,
the little blondie.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.334
-That's Penny. And Kevin.

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:14.934
So, I want to thank
Anthony Rizzo

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.968
and I want to thank Kevin for
getting Aaron Judge to sign --

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:20.100
Great job, Kevin.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:24.100
Good boy. Good boy.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.467
They also made an
announcement --

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:28.501
another announcement --
while you re-signed,

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:32.234
is that you're the 16th captain
of the New York Yankees.

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:35.300
That is a massive deal, I mean,
if you think about that list.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.501
Did you know that was coming?

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.934
And did you go like --
Did you feel that?

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.968
Did you hear rumors that
that was going to happen?

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.434
-You know, it was a shock to me.

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:44.801
You know, you always --
you know, you always dream about

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:47.033
something like that,
getting an opportunity to,

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.868
you know, represent the Yankees
and be the captain.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.300
You know, I didn't think it
would ever happen,

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.300
but, you know, I was on the
phone with Hal, the boss,

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.601
and, you know, we were kind of
talking over and negotiating

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:55.901
the deal.

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:58.534
Then, at the very end,
he's like, "Oh, by the way,

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:01.267
I'm going to name you
16th captain."

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:02.734
So it was -- I was speechless.

00:03:02.734 --> 00:03:04.067
I really didn't know
what to say.

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:06.634
But it was, you know,
an honor I don't take lightly.

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:09.534
-Not since Derek Jeter.
-Oh, yeah. Correct, correct.

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:12.234
-Have you talked to Derek
about this, this responsibility?

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:13.400
-I talked to him a little bit.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.634
Throughout the
free-agency process,

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:18.567
we talked, and really
asked about his advice,

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:20.067
what was it like for him,
you know,

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:22.434
through arbitration stuff,
free agency?

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.634
And, you know, he said,
"You know what?

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:26.467
I'll take you -- I'll take you
out for lunch or something.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:27.634
We'll kind of
talk about things."

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:29.501
But then, after I signed
my deal, he said,

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:30.667
"Well, now you're going to
take me out for

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.167
breakfast, lunch,
and dinner," so...

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:33.934
-Yeah. "Buy the restaurant,

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:37.434
and then I'll meet you at
the restaurant."

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:38.667
Unbelievable season.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:41.634
You hit an American League
record 62 home runs.

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.200
You were named the MVP.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.234
You're always focused when
you're on the on-deck circle.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:49.501
And I respect you.
I love watching you play.

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.934
And, now and then,
I go to the games,

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.033
and I -- It's just interesting.

00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:54.133
I just figured,
while you're here,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.901
I just --
You never look over at me.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:58.033
You never go like...

00:03:58.033 --> 00:03:59.934
"Jimbo! Jimbo!"

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:01.901
Nothing. Nothing.
None of that stuff.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:03.801
Never -- You just get
all business with you.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:04.901
-No. Hold on, Jimmy.

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:06.601
Hold on, hold on,
hold on, hold on.

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:08.767
I try,
but every time I look over,

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:10.567
you're taking selfies,
you're eating hot dogs,

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:11.934
you're drinking a beer.

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:13.200
I don't want to interrupt that.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.734
-No. Oh, please. Yeah, right.
-I'm just saying.

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:17.534
I'm looking. I'm looking.
-You are?

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:20.033
You do -- I think
the last game I saw you,

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:24.234
you looked -- You were doing --
You walked out and you went...

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:26.300
So I took that -- I was like --

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.367
And everybody around was like,
"Yo, he looked at you!"

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:29.601
And I go, "Alright, chill out."

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:32.467
But I mean, I'm right --

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:36.968
You have to walk in front of me
to bat and you --

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.267
You know how hard
that must be for you

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:39.868
to not acknowledge me at all?

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.200
-No.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.100
-I mean,
'cause the dugout is there.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.667
You come out
of the dugout, right?

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.133
So you come out,
and they go, "Aaron Judge."

00:04:46.133 --> 00:04:47.267
Everyone goes nuts.

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.334
And you're like --
You hit whatever,

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:50.868
the dirt out of your cleats.

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:53.567
And you -- I'm where you are.

00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:55.200
So you're kind of
already facing me

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.834
and you still don't look at me.

00:04:56.834 --> 00:05:03.767
And then you go to home plate
and you go...

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:06.100
I'm right there,
and you purposely don't even --

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.033
I go, "Okay, I'm cool,"
'cause I don't want to

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.968
freak you out and then go like,
"Hey, bud"

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:12.868
or anything or get -- I want you
to hit homers and win the game.

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:14.634
So I'm like,
"Don't even look at me."

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:16.100
Would you like me
to not look at you?

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.267
-I need a wave.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:18.767
I need a wave,
something to start --

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:20.968
-I'm only waving.
I'm waving so much.

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:23.801
It's like I'm freaking out.
I'm like -- I got a hot dog.

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:25.267
I'm like -- I got the selfie.

00:05:25.267 --> 00:05:27.000
I'm getting a selfie of me
waving at you.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.634
Like, "Look at us."

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:30.601
Look, I love you.

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:32.467
-I'm checking the tapes.
I'm going to go back.

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.200
I'm going to check the tapes.
-Alright, watch the tapes.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.334
I know you can't,
because you're you,

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:38.767
but I will tell you that
everybody in that stadium

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:40.133
loves you so much, buddy.

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:42.767
And when you
go up to that home plate,

00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:44.834
everyone's like,
"Drop whatever you're doing."

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:47.200
Just look at you and just go,
"He's the best."

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.734
You're just the coolest, man.
So I am just a big fan.

00:05:49.734 --> 00:05:51.100
But I just want to let you know.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:56.100
You know that,
but I'm in the crowd...

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.167
"Go, Aaron!

00:05:57.167 --> 00:05:58.400
Go, buddy!

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:01.701 --> 00:06:03.701
Hey, man!
-Just something.

00:06:03.701 --> 00:06:07.501
-"Known you forever," yeah.

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.901
Everyone has superstitions.

00:06:09.901 --> 00:06:11.868
Do you have one
that you can tell us

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:15.200
or do you have any secret one
you want to get off your chest

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:18.267
or have you had one
since you were a kid?

00:06:18.267 --> 00:06:21.400
-One that comes to mind
is bubble gum.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.133
So, Dubble Bubble,
two pieces before the game.

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:28.200
Throw it in, run out to the
field, warm up, play defense,

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.334
come in for my first at bat.

00:06:29.334 --> 00:06:30.367
-Uh-huh.

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:32.100
-If I get out, "Now, hold on.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.234
It can't be --
I'm not the reason I got out.

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:35.367
It's got to be this dang --"

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:37.767
-You think it's the --
It's the gum.

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:39.000
-It's the gum.
-So you spit out the gum.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.868
-Put it in the trash,
start with a new piece,

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:43.067
and hopefully that has
the mojo, you know?

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:45.033
So that's all I'm really --

00:06:45.033 --> 00:06:46.400
-It's bubble gum?

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:47.934 --> 00:06:50.868
Also, Dubble Bubble.
-Yeah.

00:06:50.868 --> 00:06:52.667
-Dubble Bubble
is kind of a workout.

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:54.067
That's kind of a jaw workout.

00:06:54.067 --> 00:06:55.267
-Yeah, I got to work on
the jawline.

00:06:55.267 --> 00:06:56.767
-I mean -- Yeah, you got --

00:06:56.767 --> 00:06:59.167
That's what I'm missing
my whole life.

00:06:59.167 --> 00:07:00.767
Oh, my gosh.
I should have done that.

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:04.801
When you walk out, everyone has
a good walkout song,

00:07:04.801 --> 00:07:06.601
a walk-on song.

00:07:06.601 --> 00:07:09.534
What is your walk-up song --
or what was it last year?

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:12.634
-This past year,
it was "Hello" by Pop Smoke.

00:07:12.634 --> 00:07:14.667
-Yeah, that was --
-It got the people going.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.868
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:18.267
-Do you -- Is that --

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:20.834
Do you have other choices
in case that one's not your one?

00:07:20.834 --> 00:07:22.701
Like, have you ever
walked out and you go,

00:07:22.701 --> 00:07:24.267
"Ooh, that was
kind of a mistake"?

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:27.501
-Well, this is by far
the toughest decision

00:07:27.501 --> 00:07:30.467
any baseball player
has to make in the off-season.

00:07:30.467 --> 00:07:33.300
I'm telling you, it's --
I make a whole playlist.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.501
I have about 30, 40 songs.
I'm in my car.

00:07:35.501 --> 00:07:36.868
My wife gets mad at me,
because she's like --

00:07:36.868 --> 00:07:38.167
I'll be sitting in there.

00:07:38.167 --> 00:07:39.434
I'll be like, "Okay, honey.
This one, this one."

00:07:39.434 --> 00:07:41.868
I'll be like, "Now batting,
number 99, Aaron Judge,"

00:07:41.868 --> 00:07:44.734
and play it and then,
you know, start it over.

00:07:44.734 --> 00:07:46.234
And I'll be like,
"What'd you think?

00:07:46.234 --> 00:07:47.767
Was that -- Is that it?

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:49.000
No? Okay. Next one, next one."

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.267
-That's hilarious.
-Yeah, it's a long process.

00:07:51.267 --> 00:07:53.200
-She's like,
"Dude, get over yourself.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:56.300
Come on, man. Let's get to mall.
Let's go."

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:57.467
But you've got to have --
It is --

00:07:57.467 --> 00:07:59.367
It's like walking into the ring.

00:07:59.367 --> 00:08:00.501
-You've got to have
something good.

00:08:00.501 --> 00:08:01.801
-Got to have something big.

00:08:01.801 --> 00:08:03.100
-Yeah, you're coming there
and you're ignoring me,

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:04.834
and I got to get a song
to get your attention.

00:08:04.834 --> 00:08:07.267
So, you know...
-I'm there with Lorne.

00:08:07.267 --> 00:08:08.667
We're always
going crazy for you.

00:08:08.667 --> 00:08:10.434
And he's got the selfie
ready to go.

00:08:10.434 --> 00:08:11.868
I think we might have one.

00:08:11.868 --> 00:08:13.734
There's a song that might not be
on your radar here.

00:08:13.734 --> 00:08:16.067
This is --
The lyrics to the song

00:08:16.067 --> 00:08:17.667
are your first and last name.

00:08:17.667 --> 00:08:22.200
It's by a YouTube creator called
Epic Baseball Songs.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.501
Give this a try here.
This could be your walk-up song.

00:08:24.501 --> 00:08:25.634
Take a listen.

00:08:25.634 --> 00:08:27.868
-♪ Aaron Judge, Aaron Judge ♪

00:08:27.868 --> 00:08:29.801
♪ Aaron Judge it, yeah ♪

00:08:29.801 --> 00:08:31.901
♪ Aaron Judge, Aaron Judge ♪

